From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] nrf/mphalport: Give a SoftDevice build real atomic sections.

A board built with a SoftDevice (SD=s140 and the like, the XIAO nRF52840
among them) never defined MICROPY_BEGIN_ATOMIC_SECTION, so it fell back to
py/mphal.h's empty one. The scheduler's sections then exclude nothing, while
a machine.Timer callback runs straight from the interrupt and calls
micropython.schedule(). A fire that lands in mp_sched_unlock(), after it
counted an empty queue and before it wrote MP_SCHED_IDLE, leaves its
callback queued with the scheduler idle. Nothing runs it until some other
schedule() sets the scheduler pending again, which at an idle REPL is the
next key typed. machine.disable_irq() masked nothing either.

Seen on a Seeed XIAO nRF52840 Sense with a 20 ms timer that re-arms a
one-shot hardware timer from its scheduled callback: it stopped for 5 to 34
seconds at a time, every few minutes, at the REPL. With a 1 ms periodic
timer counting, 20 interrupts arrived in the 20 ms after
machine.disable_irq().

Use the SoftDevice's critical region, as nrfx_glue.h already does for the
drivers. It masks the application's interrupts and leaves the SoftDevice's
own alone, and works whether or not the SoftDevice is enabled.

diff --git a/ports/nrf/mphalport.c b/ports/nrf/mphalport.c
index 7c846b7a4..2149b644a 100644
--- a/ports/nrf/mphalport.c
+++ b/ports/nrf/mphalport.c
@@ -55,6 +55,20 @@
 #include "soc/nrfx_coredep.h"
 #endif
 
+#ifdef BLUETOOTH_SD
+#include "nrf_nvic.h"
+
+mp_uint_t mp_hal_begin_atomic_section(void) {
+    uint8_t nested;
+    sd_nvic_critical_region_enter(&nested);
+    return nested;
+}
+
+void mp_hal_end_atomic_section(mp_uint_t state) {
+    sd_nvic_critical_region_exit(state);
+}
+#endif
+
 #ifndef MICROPY_HW_STDIN_BUFFER_LEN
 #define MICROPY_HW_STDIN_BUFFER_LEN 512
 #endif
diff --git a/ports/nrf/mphalport.h b/ports/nrf/mphalport.h
index 60c651839..31b786205 100644
--- a/ports/nrf/mphalport.h
+++ b/ports/nrf/mphalport.h
@@ -39,6 +39,16 @@
 #ifndef BLUETOOTH_SD
 #define MICROPY_BEGIN_ATOMIC_SECTION()     disable_irq()
 #define MICROPY_END_ATOMIC_SECTION(state)  enable_irq(state)
+#else
+// A SoftDevice build masks the application's interrupts the way the
+// SoftDevice allows, which works whether or not it has been enabled. Without
+// this the section is empty: a timer interrupt that schedules a callback can
+// then land inside mp_sched_unlock() and leave the callback queued with the
+// scheduler idle, and machine.disable_irq() masks nothing.
+mp_uint_t mp_hal_begin_atomic_section(void);
+void mp_hal_end_atomic_section(mp_uint_t state);
+#define MICROPY_BEGIN_ATOMIC_SECTION()     mp_hal_begin_atomic_section()
+#define MICROPY_END_ATOMIC_SECTION(state)  mp_hal_end_atomic_section(state)
 #endif
 
 static inline void enable_irq(mp_uint_t state) {
-- 
